\\n\\n# Slack Thread: License AGPL Reopen\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-12\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:14] Diana**: Reopening the license review. The PDF parser Evan swapped in to clear the earlier audit finding turns out to be AGPL-licensed.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 10:01] Alice**: AGPL is a dealbreaker for how we distribute this. Are we sure about the licensing?\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 10:03] Diana**: Sure — checked the license file directly. It's not something we can ship under our current distribution model.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 10:31] Charlie**: Is there a non-copyleft alternative that covers the same parsing we need?\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 10:33] Alice**: Please look.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 11:08] Diana**: Looking now. Putting this back in progress until we land on a replacement that passes a clean scan.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 40 slack thread licens agpl reopen channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 12 2026 08 12 09 14 diana reopen the licens review the pdf parser evan swap in to clear the earlier audit find turn out to be agpl licens 2026 08 12 1001 alic agpl is a dealbreak for how we distribut this are we sure about the licens 2026 08 12 1003 diana sure check the licens file direct it s not someth we can ship under our current distribut model 2026 08 12 10 31 charli is there a non copyleft altern that cover the same pars we need 2026 08 12 10 33 alic pleas look 2026 08 12 11 08 diana look now put this back in progress until we land on a replac that pass a clean scan\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e92f5d6c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-license-agpl-reopen.md\", \"id\": \"2465ca3c92b0e407\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.40493909463547784, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.239648049479254, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7906182, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-license-agpl-reopen.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e92f5d6c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-license-agpl-reopen.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-license-agpl-reopen.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 813, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:30\", \"token_count\": 257, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-11\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Handshake Protocol Deep Dive\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-22\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nDiana walked the high-latency handshake timeout. The team left handshake work blocked; no timeout-bump workaround. Path still depends on the encryption workstream.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-11\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Handshake Protocol Deep Dive\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-22\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Diana**: Handshake triage — nominal latency was fine; Bob's earlier validation held up on the local network. On a simulated high-latency link the handshake never finishes. It times out.\\n\\n**Bob**: That matches what I expected once we left the happy path. The prototype assumed round trips stay quick. High latency breaks the exchange.\\n\\n**Charlie**: Is this an encryption cost problem? AES-256 on the wire path is in the dependency chain here.\\n\\n**Bob**: It's related. The handshake still has to complete under that load, and on a slow link it doesn't. I don't have a fix that keeps the current exchange as-is.\\n\\n**Evan**: Bumping timeouts just hides it. If the link is slow enough, we still fail.\\n\\n**Diana**: I'll leave the high-latency repro in place so we can re-check when encryption or the handshake design changes.\\n\\n**Alice**: Then we leave it. Handshake work stays blocked on timeouts under high latency. It depends on the encryption path, and we're not inventing a workaround in this meeting.\\n\\n**Bob**: Agreed — no timeout bump. We'll revisit when the crypto path moves.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 11 firefli transcript handshak protocol deep dive date 2026 09 22 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop summari diana walk the high latenc handshak timeout the team left handshak work block no timeout bump workaround path still depend on the encrypt workstream sourc id src meet 11 firefli transcript handshak protocol deep dive date 2026 09 22 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop transcript diana handshak triag nomin latenc wa fine bob s earlier valid held up on the local network on a simul high latenc link the handshak never finish it time out bob that match what i expect onc we left the happi path the prototyp assum round trip stay quick high latenc break the exchang charli is this an encrypt cost problem ae 256 on the wire path is in the depend chain here bob it s relat the handshak still ha to complet under that load and on a slow link it doesn t i don t have a fix that keep the current exchang ais evan bump timeout just hide it if the link is slow enough we still fail diana i ll leav the high latenc repro in place so we can re check when encrypt or the handshak design chang alic then we leav it handshak work stay block on timeout under high latenc it depend on the encrypt path and we re not invent a workaround in this meet bob agre no timeout bump we ll revisit when the crypto path move\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e940b5088a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"id\": \"edcdc1df7188b1a3\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.40186300708662054, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.2948146786951722, \"vector_similarity\": 0.65164244, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e940b5088a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1463, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:18\", \"token_count\": 417, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-24\\n\\n# Third-Party License Inventory Report\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2024\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-09; notes status through 2026-08-15)\\n\\nRetrospective report on the third-party license audit under CIPH-40.\\n\\n## Scope of the 2026-08-09 inventory\\n\\nAn audit of the dependency tree was run to catalog every third-party license in use ahead of release, flagging anything more restrictive than a permissive license.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-24\\n\\n# Third-Party License Inventory Report\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2024\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-09; notes status through 2026-08-15)\\n\\nRetrospective report on the third-party license audit under CIPH-40.\\n\\n## Finding and immediate action\\n\\nThe PDF-parsing dependency's license was flagged as a concern, and the team 