r our current distribut model 2026 08 12 10 31 charli is there a non copyleft altern that cover the same pars we need 2026 08 12 10 33 alic pleas look 2026 08 12 11 08 diana look now put this back in progress until we land on a replac that pass a clean scan\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e92f5d6c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-license-agpl-reopen.md\", \"id\": \"2465ca3c92b0e407\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3623191922018387, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.17149874600262682, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8075669, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-license-agpl-reopen.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e92f5d6c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-license-agpl-reopen.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-license-agpl-reopen.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 813, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:30\", \"token_count\": 257, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-41\\n\\n# Dependency Inventory: License Compliance Audit (Q3) — Reopened\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2041\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (reflects reopen activity through 2026-08-15)\\n\\n## Original Finding: Ghostscript (AGPLv3)\\n\\nThe initial audit flagged `Ghostscript`, used by the `rasterizer` module for PDF-to-image conversion, as AGPLv3-licensed — on the corporate license blacklist because of its viral copyleft terms for any binary distributed to partner sites.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-41\\n\\n# Dependency Inventory: License Compliance Audit (Q3) — Reopened\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2041\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (reflects reopen activity through 2026-08-15)\\n\\n## First Remediation and Reopen\\n\\nThe team swapped in an alternative PDF parser library to replace the Ghostscript dependency, and that swap was initially marked Completed. On follow-up review, however, the replacement library itself turned out to also be AGPL-licensed — the swap solved the specific Ghostscript dependency but reintroduced the same license category problem one layer down. The task was reopened.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-41\\n\\n# Dependency Inventory: License Compliance Audit (Q3) — Reopened\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2041\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (reflects reopen activity through 2026-08-15)\\n\\n## Current Status: Unresolved\\n\\nCharlie is now searching for an Apache 2.0 or MIT-licensed PDF parser alternative that meets the module's rasterization requirements. No suitable replacement has been confirmed yet, so this audit item remains **Active (Reopened)** — not resolved.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-41\\n\\n# Dependency Inventory: License Compliance Audit (Q3) — Reopened\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2041\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (reflects reopen activity through 2026-08-15)\\n\\n## Secondary Open Item\\n\\nTesseract OCR itself is Apache 2.0, but the `eng.traineddata` model files were sourced from a community repository and their training-corpus provenance has not been verified as public-domain/CC0. This remains a separate, lower-priority open item pending Evan's trace of the `tessdata_best` provenance.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 41 depend inventori licens complianc audit q3 reopen owner diana document key doc 2041 last updat 2026 08 21 reflect reopen activ through 2026 08 15 origin find ghostscript agplv3 the initi audit flag ghostscript use by the raster modul for pdf